# Review required on the paths where a silent break costs a competition day.
#
# Deliberately narrow. Broad code-owner rules stall a volunteer team; these four
# areas are the ones where a mistake is invisible until the robot is on the field.
#
# WHO: the programming mentors for this season. Six handles, five people - one of
# them runs two accounts, and both are listed so a review request reaches him
# whichever he is signed into.
#
# This is also the pool the season-standup skill assigns issues to, which is why
# it is scoped to mentors actively doing software rather than to every admin: an
# inactive admin assigned an issue is a silently stalled task, and a code-owner
# review from someone with no basis to judge a dependency lock either blocks the
# PR or becomes a rubber stamp. Either way the gate stops meaning anything.
#
# NOTE: this file only has teeth once branch protection on `master` is set to
# "Require review from Code Owners". Until then it is advisory.
#
# A misspelled handle, or one without repository access, silently matches NOBODY
# rather than erroring. Check changes here against the collaborator list by eye.

